      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-05-26T20:51:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Fugue State Parse certainly--her damage is usually worthless, more deck manipulation makes her even better.</p><p>F5 AZ and Bunker. &nbsp;I like playing AZ a lot, but with his buildup period, he's not usually a good choice. &nbsp;F5 changes that dramatically. &nbsp;Bunker, I don't love, but his F5 version is an order of magnitude better than any other.</p><p>Extremist Sky-Scraper looks strategically interesting, and a very different way of playing that character, given that she has no other cards that grant powers.</p>",
